Package: libkrun2
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: libkrunfw5
Description: Virtualization-based process isolation library
 libkrun lets a program run processes in a partially isolated environment
 using hardware virtualization: KVM on Linux, HVF on macOS and WHP on
 Windows. It embeds the userspace side of the hypervisor and the minimum set
 of virtio devices a container-like workload needs, and exposes a C API.
 .
 The guest kernel is loaded from libkrunfw at run time.

Package: libkrun-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libkrun2 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for libkrun
 Headers and pkg-config metadata for building programs that embed libkrun.

Package: libkrun-init0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Guest init configuration library for libkrun
 Host-side library that builds the configuration a libkrun guest needs and
 injects it, together with the PID 1 binary it embeds, into the guest
 filesystem overlay. It also converts OCI container specifications into guest
 initialization structures.

Package: libkrun-init-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libkrun-init0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for the libkrun guest init library
 Headers and pkg-config metadata for building programs against
 libkrun_init.
